# Distro packaging PRs — do not spam

`techievena` already filed a burst of graft packaging PRs on 2026-09-17.
Several were closed as premature, not-notable, or wrong process. Maintainers
notice volume, duplicate PRs, Cursor trailers, and CI retriggers more than
they notice a missing Signed-off-by.

This session does **not** open, push, force-push, rebase, comment on, reopen,
or close a packaging PR against a foreign distro unless the user names that
exact repository in this session.

## Never

- Open a second PR for the same package (`openwrt/packages` #30552 then #30553).
- Force-push a distro PR branch except when **that repo's bot, on that same
  PR**, says to amend and `git push --force-with-lease` — then do it **on
  that PR**, once. Do not open a replacement PR.
- Push a follow-up commit that retriggers Homebrew bottles, nixpkgs ofborg,
  or OpenWrt multi-arch builds unless a maintainer asked for that exact fix.
- Comment on a closed PR. Do not argue notability, nascency, or process.
- File SlackBuilds **GitHub** PRs for new packages (use slackbuilds.org/submit).
- File Solus PRs without their package-request issue first.
- File brew-core until github.com/eonik-ai/graft meets Homebrew notability.
- File GitHub PRs against `gentoo/guru` (mail / Codeberg).
- Put `Made with Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, pkg.bot, or GTM copy in
  a distro PR body or commit.

## If a maintainer already objected

Stop. Leave Void #62574, Homebrew #311719, SlackBuilds #17783 closed.
Do not "fix" MacPorts #34726, Solus #10718, or OpenWrt #30553 unless the
user explicitly asks to close or reply on that URL.

nixpkgs #564184 and FreeBSD #624: wait. No pings, no extra commits.
